rnoon. A heavy sultry air. And a heavy sun. So heavy, it heaves and labours=
 in a sky blue liquid, unmoving like liquid mercury. The shadows evaporated=
 and are vacationing in another hemisphere. The air is suspended in limbo, =
unmoving. Time warps and slows; drones on, lethargic.

Footsteps. A clink. A lush gurgle of liquid. An icy transparent liquid fill=
s a crystal glass. Clear orange liquid. Ice cubes plop in. A citrus twang. =
Spears of light spike the crystal liquid with starry glint. Liquid touches =
tongue and the dense afternoon inertia breaks and shatters into infinite sh=
ards.
Infinite bursts of icy orange zest.
Infinite spears of citric light.

Is this what  the stars taste like?
